<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<sdf version="1.6">
  <world name="marc_sidewalk_driveway">

    <!-- ============================================================
         MARC / Longwood Rd S sidewalk == driveway crossing template
         Built for: VSLAM-Based Navigation for Autonomous Sidewalk Robots
                    (Mitacs Globalink 2026, Project 50124)

         DIMENSIONS AND PROVENANCE (unchanged from the source file == these
         are sourced numbers and are deliberately not second-guessed here):
           - Walkway zone width  2.0 m   -> Hamilton Complete Streets
                                            Design Guidelines (2022),
                                            target range 1.8-2.0 m
           - Buffer zone width   1.0 m   -> same source, target 1.0 m
           - Curb height         0.15 m  -> generic N.A. curb-reveal
                                            convention, NOT Hamilton-
                                            specific, verify if it matters
           - Driveway width      6.5 m   -> UNVERIFIED PLACEHOLDER for a
                                            two-way commercial driveway.
                                            Replace with a measured value
                                            from Street View or pacing it
                                            out at MARC.
           - Route length        26 m    -> arbitrary, matches the earlier
                                            plan-view sketch

         Axes: +X = direction of travel along the sidewalk (0 to 26 m)
               +Y = across the right-of-way, 0 at the building frontage,
                    increasing toward the road
               Driveway crossing centred at X=13, spanning X=9.75-16.25

         ============================================================
         WHAT CHANGED FROM THE SOURCE FILE, AND WHY
         ============================================================
         The source flagged that its material names were unverified. They
         were checked against this Jetson's
         /usr/share/gazebo-11/media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material:

           Gazebo/Concrete   DOES NOT EXIST  -> Gazebo/Pedestrian (sidewalk.jpg)
           Gazebo/Asphalt    DOES NOT EXIST  -> Gazebo/Road / Gazebo/Motorway
           Gazebo/Grass      exists, textured   (kept)
           Gazebo/Bricks     exists, textured   (kept)

         Left unfixed, the walkway, driveway apron and roadway == three of
         the six surfaces, including the one the robot drives on == would
         have rendered untextured. That is not cosmetic. A stereo camera
         tracks motion by matching small patterns between frames; an
         untextured surface yields none. Measured on this exact setup, an
         untextured world gave 13 usable keypoints in a 1920x1200 image
         against the 20 that RTAB-Map needs, and odometry failed on every
         frame. See ENGINEERING_NOTES.md.

         Three further changes for the same reason:

         1. LONG SLABS ARE TILED. Gazebo paints one copy of a texture across
            each face of a box, so the original single 26 m walkway would
            have stretched one image over the whole route and washed out all
            detail. Each surface is now built from ~2 m segments, and the
            paving alternates irregularly so the run never becomes a
            repeating pattern (identical repeating tiles cause ambiguous
            feature matching == many matches, almost none geometrically
            consistent).

         2. THE CURB IS TEXTURED. It was ambient/diffuse grey, i.e. a flat
            colour, which contributes no features at all.

         3. STREET FURNITURE ADDED. Poles, signs, a hydrant and a bin, all
            in the buffer zone and clear of the 2.0 m walkway. Loop closure
            recognises places by appearance; a bare corridor of repeating
            paving gives it nothing distinctive to key on. Spacing is
            deliberately irregular for the same reason.

         ============================================================
         GEOMETRY QUESTIONS THIS FILE DOES NOT DECIDE == see notes below
         ============================================================
         The walkway and roadway are coplanar here (both top at z=0.02),
         with the 0.15 m curb standing between them as a wall. On a real
         street the walkway sits ~0.15 m ABOVE the road and the curb is that
         reveal. Also, the walkway is perfectly level == no cross-slope ==
         and the driveway apron is flush and flat.

         That makes this world FLAT, which matters for one specific
         experiment: it cannot test what Reg/Force3DoF costs, because
         nothing here violates the flat-ground assumption. Raised walkway,
         2% cross-slope and a driveway dip are all deliberately NOT added,
         because they change sourced dimensions and that is the author's
         call, not this file's. Discussed in the accompanying message.
         ============================================================ -->

    <include>
      <uri>model://sun</uri>
    </include>

    <include>
      <uri>model://ground_plane</uri>
    </include>

    <physics type="ode">
      <max_step_size>0.001</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1</real_time_factor>
      <real_time_update_rate>1000</real_time_update_rate>
    </physics>

    <!-- ==== WALKWAY ZONE ====
         2.0 m wide, full 26 m length, centred on y=1.0, top at z=0.02.
         Collision is ONE slab so the driving surface stays perfectly
         continuous (13 abutting collision boxes could catch a wheel on a
         numerical seam); the visual is tiled purely for texture detail. -->
    <model name="walkway">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <pose>13 1.0 0.01 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>26 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>

        <visual name="w01"><pose>1 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Pedestrian</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w02"><pose>3 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Steps</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w03"><pose>5 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Pedestrian</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w04"><pose>7 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/CeilingTiled</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w05"><pose>9 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Pedestrian</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w06"><pose>11 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Steps</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w07"><pose>13 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Pedestrian</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w08"><pose>15 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/CeilingTiled</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w09"><pose>17 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Pedestrian</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w10"><pose>19 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Steps</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w11"><pose>21 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Pedestrian</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w12"><pose>23 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/CeilingTiled</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="w13"><pose>25 1.0 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2 2.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Pedestrian</name></script></material></visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- ==== BUFFER ZONE ==== 1.0 m of grass, split either side of the cut -->
    <model name="buffer_zone_west">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><pose>4.875 2.5 0.01 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>9.75 1.0 0.02</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="bw1"><pose>1.22 2.5 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2.44 1.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Grass</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="bw2"><pose>3.66 2.5 0.011 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2.44 1.0 0.02</size></box></geometry>
